---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Memflex benchmarks — measured, reproducible" desc="30-ask support workload: 73.3% from memory. Rerun instructions included." path="/benchmarks">
<div class="wrap" style="padding:64px 24px 20px">
  <span class="eyebrow">Measured · reproducible</span>
  <h1>73.3% from memory.<br />Rerun it yourself.</h1>
  <p class="lead">No cherry-picked charts. Fixed workload, fresh DB, keyless backend — one script.</p>
</div>
<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="strip">
      <div><b><em>73.3%</em></b><span>asks served from memory (22/30)</span></div>
      <div><b><em>8</em></b><span>distinct reflexes learned (10 intents)</span></div>
      <div><b>~<em>0.1</em>ms</b><span>memory path (mock; 7–10s cloud LLM)</span></div>
      <div><b>₹<em>0.24</em></b><span>metered savings on 30 asks</span></div>
    </div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:44px">What we tested</h2>
    <p class="lead">30 questions customers actually ask — refunds, cancellations, delivery tracking — in English, German, Spanish and French, each asked 3 different ways. Result: 22 answered from memory at ₹0, each in about a tenth of a millisecond.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:44px">What it means for you</h2>
    <p class="lead">At 1 lakh asks a month with 70% repeats, that's roughly 70,000 free answers — about ₹21,000–35,000/month saved on LLM bills. And your users get instant replies instead of multi-second waits, which is what makes voice agents and live chat feel alive.</p>
    <details style="margin-top:22px"><summary class="muted" style="cursor:pointer;font-size:14px">Developers: reproduce these exact numbers</summary>
      <div class="codeblock" style="margin-top:12px"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>pip install memflex
python examples/support-agent.py
curl http://localhost:8000/metrics
# → hit_rate, avg_latency_ms, cost_saved_30d_inr, calibration[]</pre></div>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px">Fixed workload, fresh SQLite, keyless backend — one script, same numbers.</p>
    </details>
    <h2 style="margin-top:44px">What we don't claim</h2>
    <p class="lead">Mock-backend latency flatters the absolute numbers — the honest delta is memory-path ms vs your LLM's seconds (measured 7–10s on Ollama Cloud). Hit-rate depends on your repeat rate: FAQ/triage/extraction workloads win; unique-every-time workloads gain nothing. Calibration numbers are self-reported from hit consistency until a third-party multilingual split exists.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
